ntel and Emerson, consistently show Jackson ahead, with an average margin near four to five points. Prediction markets give Jackson roughly an 86 to 90 percent chance of winning, and several expert raters moved the race to Lean or Likely Democratic in the race's final days.\n\nCollins retains real strengths: long incumbency, a reputation for independence, and strong fundraising, and a few raters still call the race a tossup. But Jackson has actually out-raised her, outside spending is modest on both sides, and the polling consensus has been stable for weeks. The forecast expects Jackson to win by a mid-single-digit margin, with enough uncertainty that Collins cannot be fully ruled out.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.7341, "margin": 3.16}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.6906, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.626, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.6915, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.5751, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.6364, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.6474, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.6668, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.6495, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.6328, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.6994, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.6388, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.6279, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.5727, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.6061, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.6059, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.6373, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.6384, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.6413, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.6281, "margin": 2.2}, {"date": "2026-10-12", "p_dem": 0.7044, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-13", "p_dem": 0.6795, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-14", "p_dem": 0.6677, "margin": 2.5}, {"d